\lispPackageChapter{livermore/xcs-predicate}

The \texttt{livermore/xcs-predicate} package is the protocol for a single
allele of an XCS condition.  Ternary bits, sets, intervals, and time-series
paths are all subclasses of \texttt{xcs-predicate}.  Specialize the generics
below for a new representation.

\section{Classes}

\lispClassSubsection{xcs-predicate}

The empty base class.  Make a subclass for each representation.

\section{Generics}

\lispGenericSubsection{cover}

Generate a covering predicate that matches \lispVar{situation}.  This is the
operation used by \texttt{generate-covering-classifier}.

\lispSyntax

\texttt{(cover \lispVar{predicate} \lispVar{situation} \lispVar{learning-parameters})}

A method on \texttt{symbol} builds an instance of that class and covers with
it, so \texttt{(cover 'ternary-predicate situation lp)} is legal.

\lispGenericSubsection{covering-score}

A numeric score for how general the predicate is.  Used when choosing
subsumers.

\lispSyntax

\texttt{(covering-score \lispVar{predicate} \lispVar{learning-parameters})}

The default method returns $0$.

\lispGenericSubsection{covering?}

True if the predicate matches every possible situation.

\lispSyntax

\texttt{(covering? \lispVar{predicate})}

The default method returns false.

\lispGenericSubsection{identical?}

True if \lispVar{a} and \lispVar{b} are the same for all situations.

\lispSyntax

\texttt{(identical? \lispVar{a} \lispVar{b})}

\lispGenericSubsection{match?}

True if \lispVar{predicate} matches \lispVar{situation}.  The default method
signals an error; subclasses must specialize it.

\lispSyntax

\texttt{(match? \lispVar{predicate} \lispVar{situation})}

\lispGenericSubsection{more-general?}

True if \lispVar{general} is strictly more general than \lispVar{specific}.

\lispSyntax

\texttt{(more-general? \lispVar{general} \lispVar{specific})}

\lispGenericSubsection{mutate}

Mutate \lispVar{predicate} according to \lispVar{learning-parameters},
preserving a match on \lispVar{situation}.  The default method signals an
error.

\lispSyntax

\texttt{(mutate \lispVar{predicate} \lispVar{situation} \lispVar{learning-parameters})}

\lispGenericSubsection{duplicate}

Return a newly created copy.  The default method copies a \texttt{value} slot
if one exists.
